# Ad-hoc developer scratch scripts — REPOSITORY ROOT ONLY (INFRA-499).
#
# The leading `/` is load-bearing. Unanchored, these globs match at every
# depth and swallow the permanent guard scripts in app/scripts/ and scripts/
# — silently, because `git add .` simply does not stage an ignored file and
# reports nothing, so the miss first surfaces as a red CI step invoking a
# file that is not in the repository. Anchoring keeps the original
# scratch-file intent and makes app/scripts/ and scripts/ tracked by default,
# which retired the 13 hand-written negation entries this block used to carry.
# Adding a guard script now needs no .gitignore change at all; if one is ever
# re-ignored, `npm run check:workflow-scripts` fails on the PR that does it.
/cleanup-*.js
/cleanup-*.py
/cleanup-*.sh
/cleanup_*.js
/cleanup_*.py
/cleanup_*.sh
/migrate-*.js
/migrate-*.py
/migrate-*.sh
/migration-*.js
/migration-*.py
/migration-*.sh
/validate-*.js
/validate-*.py
/validate_*.js
/validate_*.py
/verify-*.js
/verify-*.py
/check-*.js
/check-*.py
/execute-*.js
/execute-*.py
/batch_*.py
/final_*.py

